comments.body:
@Honny1 AFAICT Podman’s `main` branch has not updated Buildah after https://github.com/podman-container-tools/buildah/security/advisories/GHSA-3528-5p26-cf44 ; this report suggests that either that security fix, or a related change , has been broken _on the stable branches_.

My guess is https://github.com/podman-container-tools/buildah/pull/7077 / https://github.com/podman-container-tools/buildah/pull/7081 , see the discussion in https://github.com/podman-container-tools/buildah/pull/7077#discussion_r3936389000 . The CVE fix used to contain a unit test that “absolute and escaping symbolic links are resolved relative to the root”, and that was removed because of these changes.

OTOH, to be fair, I spent a whole day trying to find a symlink reproducer where those changes actually break `podman cp`, and I couldn’t find one — ultimately `podman cp` seems to be doing its own symlink resolution of some kind. So I might very well be missing something.
